{{ 'wb-marquee.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'wb-reels.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<section class="wb-banded wb-overflow-hidden-x">
  <div class="wb-container">
    <div class="wb-padding">
      {%- comment -%}
        Items are rendered twice — the duplicate set is what makes the loop
        seamless (see assets/wb-marquee.css). Duration is one full pass of a
        single set. Seconds per item, not a fixed total, so adding a review
        makes the strip longer rather than faster.

        The multiplier is the speed knob — smaller is faster — but set it from
        pixels per second, not by feel. Duration is one pass of one set, so the
        speed is (item count x (item width + gap)) / duration, and the strip
        also REPEATS every `duration` seconds. Push the speed too high and a
        short strip cycles in a few seconds and reads as jumping back rather
        than scrolling; that is what 0.25 here did to the 21-logo row (1360px/s,
        a full repeat every 5.25s).

        All four strips are tuned to roughly 450px/s at a 1400px viewport, which
        is about four times Glide's old pace and still repeats slowly enough to
        look continuous. Recalculate rather than nudge: the other three knobs
        live in about-content, wb-collaborate and wb-image-reel-markup, and the
        same number means a different speed in each because the item widths and
        counts differ.
      {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign marquee_count = section.blocks.size -%}
      <div
        class="wb-marquee wb-testimonials"
        style="--wb-marquee-count: {{ marquee_count }}"
      >
        <ul class="wb-marquee__track wb-reviews" role="list">
          {%- for i in (1..2) -%}
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              <li
                class="wb-marquee__item wb-review"
                style="background-image: url({{ block.settings.stars_image | asset_url }})"
                {% if forloop.parentloop.index == 2 %}aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}
                {% if forloop.parentloop.index == 1 %}{{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}
              >
                {{ block.settings.review_text }}
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Reviews",
  "settings": [],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "review",
      "name": "Review",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "review_text",
          "label": "Review text",
          "default": "Great service and amazing product!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "stars_image",
          "label": "Stars image filename",
          "default": "wb-stars.gif",
          "info": "Upload image to assets folder and enter filename here"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
